{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_w2mdvdztrwhtvng3shlxyzo6i2t3qkmb4zhnkiugse5gqr5zeanq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_013t56Kdfy9G1GDyk2iiE9Vo","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QGr4ci/translation/SYMBOLS.md","content":"# Phase A.1 — Symbol surface\n\nDerived mechanically from `nm -D` on both shared libraries.\n\n* C: `c_src/build/lib<project>.so`, built exactly as the task specifies\n  (`cmake .. -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON && cmake --build .`).\n  No `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, therefore **`-O0` with `assert()` enabled**.\n* Rust: `translation/target/release/libload_png_mem_lib.so` (`crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`).\n\nRegenerate with `./build_diff.sh` then `cargo test --test symbols`, which fails\nif the two `nm -D` sets ever differ.\n\n## Exported (dynamic, defined) symbols\n\n`nm -D -S --defined-only`, sorted by name. `size` is the ELF symbol size.\n\n| # | symbol | C type | Rust type | C size | Rust size | translated in |\n|---|--------|--------|-----------|--------|-----------|---------------|\n| 1 | `cp_dist_base`         | `D` (.data) | `D` | 0x80  | 0x80  | `src/lib.rs` `static mut cp_dist_base` |\n| 2 | `cp_dist_extra_bits`   | `D` (.data) | `D` | 0x20  | 0x20  | `src/lib.rs` `static mut cp_dist_extra_bits` |\n| 3 | `cp_error_reason`      | `B` (.bss)  | `B` | 0x08  | 0x08  | `src/lib.rs` `static mut cp_error_reason` |\n| 4 | `cp_fixed_table`       | `D` (.data) | `D` | 0x140 | 0x140 | `src/lib.rs` `static mut cp_fixed_table` |\n| 5 | `cp_inflate`           | `T` (.text) | `T` | —     | —     | `src/lib.rs` `pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn cp_inflate` |\n| 6 | `cp_len_base`          | `D` (.data) | `D` | 0x7c  | 0x7c  | `src/lib.rs` `static mut cp_len_base` |\n| 7 | `cp_len_extra_bits`    | `D` (.data) | `D` | 0x1f  | 0x1f  | `src/lib.rs` `static mut cp_len_extra_bits` |\n| 8 | `cp_permutation_order` | `D` (.data) | `D` | 0x13  | 0x13  | `src/lib.rs` `static mut cp_permutation_order` |\n| 9 | `load_png_mem`         | `T` (.text) | `T` | —     | —     | `src/lib.rs` `pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn load_png_mem` |\n\n**Missing from Rust: none.** The name sets are identical, every object symbol\nhas the same size and the same section class (`.data` vs `.bss`), and both\nfunctions are `T`. There are no namespacing/renaming macros in\n`c_src/include/lib.h`, so linker names equal source-level names, and there are\nno macro-generated exports.\n\n## `static` C functions (not exported, still translated)\n\n`c_src/src/lib.c` marks the rest of the implementation `static`, so it is\ndeliberately absent from `nm -D`. All of it is nevertheless present in\n`src/lib.rs` — nothing was stubbed and no C source file was skipped\n(`c_src` contains exactly one `.c` file):\n\n| C (local `t` symbol) | Rust |\n|---|---|\n| `cp_make_pixel_a` | `cp_make_pixel_a` |\n| `cp_make_pixel` | `cp_make_pixel` |\n| `cp_would_overflow` | `cp_would_overflow` |\n| `cp_ptr` | `cp_ptr` |\n| `cp_peak_bits` | `cp_peak_bits` |\n| `cp_consume_bits` | `cp_consume_bits` |\n| `cp_read_bits` | `cp_read_bits` |\n| `cp_rev16` | `cp_rev16` |\n| `cp_build` | `cp_build` |\n| `cp_stored` | `cp_stored` |\n| `cp_fixed` | `cp_fixed` |\n| `cp_decode` | `cp_decode` |\n| `cp_dynamic` | `cp_dynamic` |\n| `cp_block` | `cp_block` |\n| `cp_paeth` | `cp_paeth` |\n| `cp_make32` | `cp_make32` |\n| `cp_chunk` | `cp_chunk` |\n| `cp_find` | `cp_find` |\n| `cp_unfilter` | `cp_unfilter` |\n| `cp_convert` | `cp_convert` |\n| `cp_get_alpha_for_indexed_image` | `cp_get_alpha_for_indexed_image` |\n| `cp_depalette` | `cp_depalette` |\n| `cp_get_chunk_byte_length` | `cp_get_chunk_byte_length` |\n| `cp_out_size` | `cp_out_size` |\n\n## Undefined (imported) symbols\n\nC imports `__assert_fail`, `calloc`, `free`, `malloc`, `memcmp`, `memcpy`,\n`memset` (plus the usual weak `_ITM_*` / `__gmon_start__` / `__cxa_finalize`).\n\nRust imports the same allocator/`mem*` entry points (`bcmp` is glibc's\n`memcmp`), plus `libstd`'s panic-runtime and `dl_iterate_phdr`/`_Unwind_*`\nsupport. **0 undefined non-libc symbols**: every remaining `U` is either glibc\nor the `libgcc`/`libstd` unwinder, all of which the dynamic loader resolves —\nverified by `dlopen`ing the library in `tests/symbols.rs`, which would fail on\nan unresolved symbol.\n\n`__assert_fail` is *not* imported by Rust: the translation reproduces the\n`NDEBUG` behaviour of the C (see `ERRORS.md`, \"assert surface\").\n\n## Type/ABI parity\n\n| item | C | Rust |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cp_pixel_t` | 4 bytes, `r,g,b,a` | `#[repr(C)]`, 4 bytes |\n| `cp_image_t` | 16 bytes, `int w; int h; cp_pixel_t *pix;` | `#[repr(C)]`, 16 bytes, returned by value in `RAX:RDX` |\n| `cp_state_t` (internal) | 2464 bytes; `lookup`@72 `lit`@1096 `dst`@2248 `len`@2376 | asserted in `src/lib.rs` unit tests |\n\n`cp_state_t`'s layout is load-bearing, not incidental: `cp_decode` reads\n`tree[-1]` when a Huffman tree is empty, i.e. it reads the *preceding* struct\nfield, so `lit`/`dst`/`len` must sit at the same offsets as in C.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3739,"cache_read_input_tokens":146255,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3739,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca950163-4526-4c83-bcdb-90a4f8c566ab","uuid":"1239cb9b-4bb9-4b66-a0cd-932e56c46ca2","timestamp":"2026-08-27T12:55:02.828Z"}
