{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6fzvcwhdp5y3ee4sor2w6dce5tjkmeme37pwtwzzetten5wxuppq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01WRSPjFsupozVUr6bUd3ytz","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QGr4ci/translation/ERRORS.md","content":"# Phase A.2 — Error-surface table\n\nEvery distinct way `c_src/src/lib.c` rejects or errors on input. Derived\nmechanically: `grep -n 'cp_error_reason =' ` (26 sites, 25 distinct strings),\n`grep -n 'return 0'` in the non-`cp_err` helpers (4 more sites),\n`grep -n 'assert('` (10 sites), plus every explicit range/null/min-max check.\n\nTests live in `tests/errors.rs`; each row's `[x]` is ticked by a named\ndifferential test that constructs exactly that condition and asserts the C and\nRust libraries return the same sentinel **and** the same `cp_error_reason`\nstring (not merely \"both failed\").\n\n`load_png_mem` signals failure by returning `img.pix == NULL` (with `img.w`,\n`img.h` left at whatever was computed before the failure — the table records\nthat too, since it is observable). `cp_inflate` signals failure with `0`.\n\n## `cp_stored` (`btype == 0`)\n\n| # | function | trigger (exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | [x] |\n|---|----------|------------------------------------------|-------------------|-----|\n| E1 | `cp_stored` L161 | `LEN != (uint16_t)~NLEN` | `cp_stored`→0, `cp_inflate`→0, reason `\"Failed to find LEN and NLEN as complements within stored (uncompressed) stream.\"` | [x] |\n| E2 | `cp_stored` L170 | `!(s->bits_left / 8 <= (int)LEN)` — i.e. more than `LEN` bytes are left in the stream, so *any* stored block that is not the last thing in the input | `cp_inflate`→0, reason `\"Stored block extends beyond end of input stream.\"` | [x] |\n\n## `cp_block` (`btype == 1` and `btype == 2`)\n\n| # | function | trigger | expected C result | [x] |\n|---|----------|---------|-------------------|-----|\n| E3 | `cp_block` L245 | literal symbol decoded while `s->out + 1 > s->out_end` (output buffer full) | `cp_inflate`→0, reason `\"Attempted to overwrite out buffer while outputting a symbol.\"` | [x] |\n| E4 | `cp_block` L264 | back-reference with `s->out - backwards_distance < s->begin` (distance reaches before the output buffer) | `cp_inflate`→0, reason `\"Attempted to write before out buffer (invalid backwards distance).\"` | [x] |\n| E5 | `cp_block` L273 | back-reference with `s->out + length > s->out_end` | `cp_inflate`→0, reason `\"Attempted to overwrite out buffer while outputting a string.\"` | [x] |\n\n## `cp_inflate`\n\n| # | function | trigger | expected C result | [x] |\n|---|----------|---------|-------------------|-----|\n| E6 | `cp_inflate` L345 | `btype == 3` (both type bits set) | `cp_inflate`→0, reason `\"Detected unknown block type within input stream.\"` | [x] |\n| E7 | `cp_inflate` L327/334/341 | `cp_stored`/`cp_block` failed (E1–E5) in any block of a multi-block stream | `cp_inflate`→0, reason from the inner failure; `free(s)` still runs | [x] |\n\n## `cp_chunk` / `cp_find` (return `NULL`, surfaced as E10/E23/E31)\n\n| # | function | trigger | expected C result | [x] |\n|---|----------|---------|-------------------|-----|\n| E8a | `cp_chunk` L381 | `memcmp(start + 4, chunk, 4) != 0` — the chunk at `png->p` is not the wanted type | returns `NULL`, `png->p` unchanged | [x] |\n| E8b | `cp_chunk` L381 | `len < minlen` (`minlen == 13` for IHDR, `0` elsewhere) | returns `NULL`, `png->p` unchanged | [x] |\n| E8c | `cp_chunk` L383 | `png->p + (int)(len + 12) > png->end`. `offset` is `int`, so `len >= 0x80000000` sign-extends and walks *backwards*, which passes the test | returns `NULL` (or succeeds with a backwards `p`) | [x] |\n| E9 | `cp_find` L393 | loop runs off the end (`png->p >= png->end`) without a matching chunk; `png->p += len + 12` is `uint32` here, so it zero-extends | returns `NULL`, `png->p` left `>= png->end` | [x] |\n\n## `cp_unfilter`\n\n| # | function | trigger | expected C result | [x] |\n|---|----------|---------|-------------------|-----|\n| E10 | `cp_unfilter` L424 | filter byte of **row 0** `> 4` (only when `h > 0`) | returns 0 → `load_png_mem` reason `\"invalid filter byte found\"`, `pix` freed → `NULL` | [x] |\n| E11 | `cp_unfilter` L458 | filter byte of **any row `y >= 1`** `> 4` | returns 0 → same reason | [x] |\n\n## `load_png_mem`\n\n| # | function | trigger | expected C result | [x] |\n|---|----------|---------|-------------------|-----|\n| E12 | L528 | first 8 bytes != `\"\\211PNG\\r\\n\\032\\n\"` (read unconditionally — even for `png_length` 0 or negative) | `pix = NULL`, `w = h = 0`, reason `\"incorrect file signature (is this a png file?)\"` | [x] |\n| E13 | L538 | `cp_chunk(&png,\"IHDR\",13) == NULL`: not an `IHDR`, or `len < 13`, or the chunk overruns `png.end` | `pix = NULL`, `w = h = 0`, reason `\"unable to find IHDR chunk\"` | [x] |\n| E14 | L548 | `ihdr[8] != 8` (any bit depth but 8: 0,1,2,4,16,255,…) | `pix = NULL`, reason `\"only bit-depth of 8 is supported\"` | [x] |\n| E15 | L571 | `ihdr[9]` not in `{0,2,3,4,6}` (1,5,7,…,255) | `pix = NULL`, reason `\"unknown color type\"` | [x] |\n| E16 | L584 | `!(w >= 1)` where `w = cp_make32(ihdr) + 1` as `int`: IHDR width `0xFFFFFFFF` → `w == 0`, or width `>= 0x7FFFFFFF` → `w` negative | `pix = NULL`, reason `\"invalid IHDR chunk found, image width was less than 1\"` | [x] |\n| E17 | L592 | `!(h >= 1)`: IHDR height `0` or `>= 0x80000000` (negative as `int`) | `pix = NULL`, reason `\"invalid IHDR chunk found, image height was less than 1\"` | [x] |\n| E18 | L601 | `!((int64_t)w * h * sizeof(cp_pixel_t) < INT_MAX)` — note the `sizeof` makes the comparison **unsigned** | `pix = NULL`, reason `\"image too large\"` | [x] |\n| E19 | L613 | `malloc(pix_bytes)` returned `NULL` | `pix = NULL`, `w`/`h` already set, reason `\"unable to allocate raw image space\"` | [x] (documented unreachable — E18 caps `pix_bytes` below `INT_MAX`; covered by an allocator-exhaustion probe) |\n| E20 | L624 | `ihdr[10] != 0` | `pix = NULL` (freed), reason `\"only standard compression DEFLATE is supported\"` | [x] |\n| E21 | L632 | `ihdr[11] != 0` | `pix = NULL`, reason `\"only standard adaptive filtering is supported\"` | [x] |\n| E22 | L640 | `ihdr[12] != 0` (interlace) | `pix = NULL`, reason `\"interlacing is not supported\"` | [x] |\n| E23 | L674 | `!(data && datalen >= 6)`: no IDAT at all (`datalen == 0`), or total IDAT bytes 1..5, or `datalen` wrapped negative so `malloc` failed | `pix = NULL`, reason `\"corrupt zlib structure in DEFLATE stream\"` | [x] |\n| E24 | L682 | `(data[0] & 0x0f) != 0x08` — zlib CM other than DEFLATE | `pix = NULL`, reason `\"only zlib compression method (RFC 1950) is supported\"` | [x] |\n| E25 | L690 | `(data[0] & 0xf0) > 0x70` — CINFO 8..15 | `pix = NULL`, reason `\"innapropriate window size detected\"` (sic) | [x] |\n| E26 | L698 | `data[1] & 0x20` — FDICT set | `pix = NULL`, reason `\"preset dictionary is present and not supported\"` | [x] |\n| E27 | L706 | `cp_out_size(&img, 4) < 1` | `pix = NULL`, reason `\"invalid image size found\"` | [x] (proved unreachable: E16/E17 force `w,h >= 1` and E18 forces `w*h*4 < INT_MAX`, so `cp_out_size(img,4) == w*h*4 >= 4`) |\n| E28 | L714 | `cp_out_size(&img, bpp) < 1` | `pix = NULL`, reason `\"invalid image size found\"` | [x] (same proof; `bpp >= 1` for all five accepted colour types) |\n| E29 | L723 | `cp_inflate(...) == 0` for any reason (E1–E7) | `pix = NULL`, reason **`\"DEFLATE algorithm failed\"`** — it *overwrites* the inner reason | [x] |\n| E30 | L731 | `cp_unfilter(...) == 0` (E10/E11) | `pix = NULL`, reason `\"invalid filter byte found\"` | [x] |\n| E31 | L740 | `color_type == 3` and no `PLTE` chunk was found | `pix = NULL`, reason `\"color type of indexed requires a PLTE chunk\"` | [x] |\n\n## Generic FFI-boundary boundaries (not distinct C branches, tested anyway)\n\n| # | entry point | trigger | expected C result | [x] |\n|---|-------------|---------|-------------------|-----|\n| G1 | `load_png_mem` | `png_data == NULL` | reads 8 bytes from address 0 → `SIGSEGV` in **both** libraries (the C has no null check) | [x] |\n| G2 | `load_png_mem` | `png_length == 0`, `1`, `7` with a valid signature prefix | signature `memcmp` still reads 8 bytes; fails at E12 or E13 | [x] |\n| G3 | `load_png_mem` | `png_length` negative (`-1`, `INT_MIN`) → `png.end < png.p` | E13 (`cp_chunk` bound fails) | [x] |\n| G4 | `load_png_mem` | `png_length` far larger than the buffer | walks off the buffer; both read the same bytes | [x] |\n| G5 | `cp_inflate` | `in_bytes == 0` (`bits_left == 0`, no words, no final word) | `count` stays 0; `cp_read_bits` reads a zero `bits` → `btype` from zeros → E2/E6/loop; deterministic and identical | [x] |\n| G6 | `cp_inflate` | `out_bytes == 0` (`out_end == out == begin`) | first literal hits E3 | [x] |\n| G7 | `cp_inflate` | `in_bytes` negative | `bits_left` negative, `word_count = (in_bytes - first)/4` negative → no words; identical | [x] |\n| G8 | `cp_inflate` | `out_bytes` negative → `out_end < out` | E3/E5 immediately | [x] |\n| G9 | `cp_inflate` | `in` at each of the 4 alignments mod 4, and each of the 4 `last_bytes` values | changes `first_bytes`/`word_count`/`final_word`; must be bit-identical | [x] |\n| G10 | `cp_inflate` | `in == NULL` with `in_bytes == 0` | `first_bytes = 0`, no dereference, behaves as G5 | [x] |\n| G11 | `load_png_mem` | `color_type` / `bit_depth` / `compression` / `filter` / `interlace` = every value 0..255 (out-of-range \"enum\" values across the FFI boundary — C enums accept any `int`) | exactly one of E14/E15/E20/E21/E22, or success | [x] |\n| G12 | `load_png_mem` | filter byte = every value 0..255 on row 0 and on row 1 | 0..4 handled, 5..255 → E10/E11 | [x] |\n| G13 | `cp_inflate` | `btype` = each of 0,1,2,3 | 3 → E6 | [x] |\n| G14 | both | a caller mutates each exported table to out-of-range values before the call | the C reads the mutated table; both must change identically | [x] |\n\n## `assert` surface (10 sites)\n\nThe reference build has **no `NDEBUG`** (`CMakeLists.txt` sets no\n`CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`), so these are live and `abort()` the process. The Rust\ntranslation reproduces the **`NDEBUG`** behaviour instead, which is what every\n`-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release/RelWithDebInfo/MinSizeRel` build does, and what a\nlibrary that must not kill its caller has to do.\n\n`tests/errors.rs::asserts_are_the_only_divergence_from_the_assert_build`\ntherefore runs each row below against **both** C builds inside a forked child\nand requires:\n\n* Rust `==` `libc_ndebug_O0.so` (the same `-O0` code, `assert()` compiled out) —\n  a hard requirement, byte for byte; and\n* the reference `libc_assert.so` either agrees too, or dies of `SIGABRT`.\n\n| # | function | trigger | reference C (asserts on) | `NDEBUG` C == Rust | [x] |\n|---|----------|---------|--------------------------|--------------------|-----|\n| A1 | `cp_ptr` L80 | `s->bits_left & 7` on entry to `cp_stored`'s `memcpy` | `SIGABRT` | copies from the unaligned pointer | [x] |\n| A2 | `cp_peak_bits` L89 | `s->word_index > s->word_count` | unreachable (guarded by the enclosing `if`) | — | [x] |\n| A3 | `cp_consume_bits` L100 | `s->count < num_bits_to_read` — stream exhausted, or `num_bits_to_read` > 32 from an out-of-range `cp_len_extra_bits` read | `SIGABRT` | consumes a short/zero-padded `bits` | [x] |\n| A4 | `cp_read_bits` L108 | `num_bits_to_read > 32`: `cp_len_extra_bits[symbol]`/`cp_dist_extra_bits[symbol]` read out of range can be up to 255 | `SIGABRT` | `1u64 << (n & 63)` mask, as x86-64 `shl` does | [x] |\n| A5 | `cp_read_bits` L109 | `num_bits_to_read < 0` | unreachable — every caller passes an unsigned/`&7`/`&0xF` value | — | [x] |\n| A6 | `cp_read_bits` L110 | `s->bits_left <= 0` — reading past the end of the input | `SIGABRT` | keeps decoding zero bits | [x] |\n| A7 | `cp_read_bits` L111 | `s->count > 64` | unreachable — `count` only grows to `<= 63`, then by 32 | — | [x] |\n| A8 | `cp_read_bits` L112 | `(s->bits_left + s->count) - num_bits < 0` | `SIGABRT` | keeps decoding | [x] |\n| A9 | `cp_build` L139 | a code length `>= 16`: `cp_dynamic` writes `(uint8_t)sym` and `sym` can be up to 4095 (see `CONFIGS.md` C24), or a caller mutates `cp_fixed_table` | `SIGABRT` | `counts/codes/first` are 256 entries here instead of 16, so no stack smash | [x] |\n| A10 | `cp_decode` L202 | the peeked bits do not match the code found by the binary search — i.e. an incomplete Huffman tree, or an empty one (`hi == 0`, which reads `tree[-1]`) | `SIGABRT` | returns `(tree[lo-1] >> 4) & 0xFFF` | [x] |\n\n## Constants and limits the C encodes\n\n| constant | value | where |\n|---|---|---|\n| PNG signature | `89 50 4E 47 0D 0A 1A 0A` | L516 |\n| IHDR minimum length | 13 | L536 |\n| PLTE/tRNS/IDAT minimum length | 0 | L648/653/659 |\n| only supported bit depth | 8 | L548 |\n| accepted colour types → bpp | 0→1, 2→3, 3→1, 4→2, 6→4 | L555-580 |\n| image size cap | `(int64_t)w*h*4 < INT_MAX` (unsigned compare) | L601 |\n| minimum zlib stream | `datalen >= 6` | L674 |\n| zlib CM | `data[0] & 0x0f == 8` | L682 |\n| zlib CINFO | `data[0] & 0xf0 <= 0x70` | L690 |\n| zlib FDICT | `data[1] & 0x20 == 0` | L698 |\n| stored block `LEN` | `uint16_t`, 0..65535 | L158 |\n| `nlit` | `257 + 5 bits` → 257..288 | L209 |\n| `ndst` | `1 + 5 bits` → 1..32 | L210 |\n| `nlen` | `4 + 4 bits` → 4..19 | L211 |\n| code-length alphabet | 19 | L208/214 |\n| `lookup` fast table | `1 << 9` entries, only for `len <= 9` | L68/143 |\n| Huffman code length | `assert(len < 16)`; `first[15]` is the tree size | L139/152 |\n| decoded symbol range | `(key >> 4) & 0xFFF` → 0..4095 | L205 |\n| run-length symbols | 16: `3 + 2 bits`, 17: `3 + 3 bits`, 18: `11 + 7 bits` | L219-230 |\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1597,"cache_read_input_tokens":152627,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1597,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca950163-4526-4c83-bcdb-90a4f8c566ab","uuid":"69def35e-c05a-4a8b-8ec5-2702639d80af","timestamp":"2026-08-27T12:56:21.699Z"}
