{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_gxz54jh5lo4vkndm2mvczelpcba2g52coykv5mfz2tzpw54rzf3q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01Lrsso66smxvDKuFYeTRfEP","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QGr4ci/translation/CONFIGS.md","content":"# Phase A.3 — Configuration-surface table\n\nThe axes `c_src/src/lib.c` actually branches on, enumerated from the source\n(`switch`/`if` on option bytes, on `bpp`, on `btype`, on filter bytes, on\npointer alignment) — not from what looks important. There are no `#ifdef`s and\nno build-time options in the C, and no Cargo features in the Rust crate, so the\nwhole surface is *runtime* configuration.\n\n## The two public entry points\n\n`c_src/include/lib.h` declares only `load_png_mem`, but the C `.so` also\nexports `cp_inflate` and six mutable tables (`SYMBOLS.md`). `cp_inflate` is the\nlow-level entry point and is driven **directly** below, not only through\n`load_png_mem`, because it is the only way to control the input pointer\nalignment, `in_bytes`/`out_bytes` independently, and multi-block streams — and\nbecause through it the whole output allocation can be diffed byte for byte\ninstead of just the `w*h` pixels `load_png_mem` converts.\n\n## Axes\n\n| axis | values the C distinguishes | source |\n|---|---|---|\n| entry point | `cp_inflate`, `load_png_mem` | — |\n| `btype` | 0 stored, 1 fixed, 2 dynamic (3 = error, `ERRORS.md` E6) | L324 |\n| block count | 1, >1 (`bfinal` loop) | L321-356 |\n| `in` alignment | `((in+3) & ~3) - in` ∈ {0,1,2,3} → `first_bytes` | L305 |\n| `last_bytes` | `(in_bytes - first_bytes) & 3` ∈ {0,1,2,3} → `final_word_available` | L308-314 |\n| `out_bytes` | exact, larger, smaller than the stream produces; 0 | L317 |\n| `colour type` | 0, 2, 3, 4, 6 → `bpp` 1, 3, 1, 2, 4 | L555-580 |\n| palette | `PLTE` absent / present; `tRNS` absent / present; `trns_len` ≤ / > index | L648-657, L485-507 |\n| filter byte | 0,1,2,3,4 — **row 0 and rows ≥ 1 run different code** | L406-461 |\n| `w * bpp` vs `bpp` | `len <= bpp` makes the second loop of each filter empty | L435-457 |\n| IDAT layout | 1 chunk; N chunks (`cp_find` then `cp_chunk`); empty chunk; chunks separated by another chunk (breaks the `cp_chunk` chain) | L659-672 |\n| chunk order | PLTE before/after tRNS, ancillary chunks in between, chunks after IDAT | L647-664 |\n| zlib header | `CM` = 8, `CINFO` = 0..7, `FDICT` = 0 | L682-704 |\n| dynamic header | `nlit` 257..288, `ndst` 1..32, `nlen` 4..19 | L209-213 |\n| code-length coding | literal lengths only, or with run symbols 16 / 17 / 18 | L216-235 |\n| `cp_build` fast path | code length ≤ 9 fills `s->lookup`, > 9 does not | L143 |\n| match distance | 1 → `memset` path; > 1 → byte-copy path | L284-291 |\n| length/dist symbols | all 29 length and all 30 distance symbols, incl. every extra-bit width | L257-262 |\n| table mutation | caller writes any of the 6 exported tables before the call | `SYMBOLS.md` |\n\n## Rows\n\nOne row per combination the C treats differently. Each is exercised with many\nrandomised inputs (fixed seed) in `tests/valid.rs`, and every byte of the\noutput allocation (`cp_inflate`) or of the `w*h` pixel block (`load_png_mem`)\nplus the return value and `cp_error_reason` must match.\n\n### `cp_inflate` directly\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|---|----------------|-------------------------------------------|-----|\n| C1 | `cp_inflate` | `btype=0` stored, payload length 0 / 1 / 2 / 3 / 4 / 5 / 17 / 255 / 1024, × `in` alignment 0-3, × `out_bytes` = exact | [x] |\n| C2 | `cp_inflate` | `btype=0` stored, `out_bytes` > payload (slack must stay untouched) | [x] |\n| C3 | `cp_inflate` | `btype=1` fixed, literals only, all four literal-code sub-ranges (0-143 → 8 bits, 144-255 → 9 bits, 256-279 → 7 bits, 280-287 → 8 bits), random payloads 0..300 bytes, × `in` alignment 0-3 | [x] |\n| C4 | `cp_inflate` | `btype=1` fixed, back-reference `dist == 1` (the `memset` fast path), every length 3..258 | [x] |\n| C5 | `cp_inflate` | `btype=1` fixed, back-reference `dist > 1` (byte-copy path), overlapping and non-overlapping, every distance symbol 0..29 with random extra bits | [x] |\n| C6 | `cp_inflate` | `btype=1` fixed, every length symbol 257..285 with random extra bits | [x] |\n| C7 | `cp_inflate` | `btype=2` dynamic, `nlit == 257` and `ndst == 1` (minimum header) | [x] |\n| C8 | `cp_inflate` | `btype=2` dynamic, `nlit == 288` and `ndst == 32` (maximum header) | [x] |\n| C9 | `cp_inflate` | `btype=2` dynamic, random `nlit` 257..288 × random `ndst` 1..32, code lengths ≤ 9 (fills `s->lookup`) | [x] |\n| C10 | `cp_inflate` | `btype=2` dynamic, code lengths > 9 present (so `cp_build` skips the `lookup` fast path for those symbols) | [x] |\n| C11 | `cp_inflate` | `btype=2` dynamic, code-length stream encoded **with** run symbols 16, 17 and 18 (all three exercised, incl. maximum runs 6 / 10 / 138) | [x] |\n| C12 | `cp_inflate` | `btype=2` dynamic, `nlen` (HCLEN+4) = 4, 5, 12, 18, 19 | [x] |\n| C13 | `cp_inflate` | `btype=2` dynamic with back-references (`dist == 1` and `dist > 1`) | [x] |\n| C14 | `cp_inflate` | multi-block: fixed+fixed, fixed+dynamic, dynamic+fixed, dynamic+dynamic, 3 and 5 blocks, `bfinal` only on the last | [x] |\n| C15 | `cp_inflate` | multi-block ending in a stored block (the only position the C accepts one) | [x] |\n| C16 | `cp_inflate` | `in_bytes` chosen so `last_bytes` = 0, 1, 2 and 3 (the `final_word` path) × `in` alignment 0-3 — 16 combinations | [x] |\n| C17 | `cp_inflate` | stream that ends exactly on a word boundary vs one that needs the final partial word | [x] |\n| C18 | `cp_inflate` | `out` alignment 0-3 (`out` has no alignment requirement, but `memset`/copy paths differ) | [x] |\n| C19 | `cp_inflate` | called repeatedly on the same `Lib` (state is heap-allocated per call; `cp_error_reason` is sticky) | [x] |\n| C20 | `cp_inflate` | after the caller mutates `cp_fixed_table` (still a valid, complete code) — changes which symbols decode | [x] |\n| C21 | `cp_inflate` | after the caller mutates `cp_len_base` / `cp_len_extra_bits` / `cp_dist_base` / `cp_dist_extra_bits` (changes lengths and distances) | [x] |\n| C22 | `cp_inflate` | after the caller mutates `cp_permutation_order` (changes which code-length slot each 3-bit field lands in) | [x] |\n| C23 | `cp_inflate` | randomised fuzz over the *valid* corpus: bit flips inside the payload that keep the stream decodable | [x] |\n| C24 | `cp_inflate` | an **empty** Huffman tree: `nlit`/`ndst` code lengths all zero, so `cp_decode` runs with `hi == 0` and reads `tree[-1]` — the preceding `cp_state_t` field. Both must return the same symbol from the same struct offsets, and the same out-of-range `cp_len_*`/`cp_dist_*` table reads | [x] |\n\n### `load_png_mem`\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|---|----------------|-------------------------------------------|-----|\n| C25 | `load_png_mem` | colour type 0 (`bpp=1`), sizes (w,h) ∈ {1,2,3,5,16}×{1,2,3,7}, filter byte 0 on all rows | [x] |\n| C26 | `load_png_mem` | colour type 2 (`bpp=3`), same size grid | [x] |\n| C27 | `load_png_mem` | colour type 4 (`bpp=2`), same size grid | [x] |\n| C28 | `load_png_mem` | colour type 6 (`bpp=4`, `out == img.pix`, fully in place), same size grid | [x] |\n| C29 | `load_png_mem` | colour type 3 + `PLTE`, no `tRNS` (`cp_depalette`, alpha 255) | [x] |\n| C30 | `load_png_mem` | colour type 3 + `PLTE` + `tRNS`, `trns_len` = 0, 1, 128, 256 and > 256 (`cp_get_alpha_for_indexed_image`'s `index >= trns_len` branch on both sides) | [x] |\n| C31 | `load_png_mem` | colour type 3 with palette indices beyond the `PLTE` payload (the C reads past the chunk — both must read the same bytes) | [x] |\n| C32 | `load_png_mem` | every filter byte 0..4 on **row 0** × every colour type (row 0 runs its own code: filter 2 is a no-op and filter 4 uses `cp_paeth(raw