beyond the `PLTE` payload (the C reads past the chunk — both must read the same bytes) | [x] |\n| C32 | `load_png_mem` | every filter byte 0..4 on **row 0** × every colour type (row 0 runs its own code: filter 2 is a no-op and filter 4 uses `cp_paeth(raw[x-bpp],0,0)`) | [x] |\n| C33 | `load_png_mem` | every filter byte 0..4 on **rows ≥ 1** × every colour type | [x] |\n| C34 | `load_png_mem` | mixed per-row filters, randomised over 0..4, h up to 9 | [x] |\n| C35 | `load_png_mem` | `w * bpp <= bpp` (i.e. `w == 1`) so each filter's second loop is empty, × all colour types | [x] |\n| C36 | `load_png_mem` | `h == 1` (the `for y in 1..h` loop never runs) | [x] |\n| C37 | `load_png_mem` | IDAT split over 2, 3, 5 and 17 chunks | [x] |\n| C38 | `load_png_mem` | a zero-length IDAT chunk at the start / middle / end | [x] |\n| C39 | `load_png_mem` | an ancillary chunk *between* two IDATs — `cp_chunk` stops there, so only the IDATs before it are used | [x] |\n| C40 | `load_png_mem` | ancillary chunks before IHDR-adjacent position, before PLTE, between PLTE and tRNS, after the last IDAT | [x] |\n| C41 | `load_png_mem` | `PLTE` present but colour type ≠ 3; `tRNS` present but colour type ≠ 3 (both parsed, neither used) | [x] |\n| C42 | `load_png_mem` | `tRNS` before `PLTE` in the file (`cp_find` for PLTE runs first and consumes it) | [x] |\n| C43 | `load_png_mem` | IHDR with `len > 13` (extra trailing bytes — accepted, `minlen` is 13) | [x] |\n| C44 | `load_png_mem` | zlib `CINFO` = 0..7 × `FDICT` = 0, `FCHECK` bits arbitrary (never validated) | [x] |\n| C45 | `load_png_mem` | IDAT payload built with `btype` 0 / 1 / 2, and with 2 blocks | [x] |\n| C46 | `load_png_mem` | DEFLATE stream producing *more* than `(w*bpp+1)*h` bytes (extra output ignored) | [x] |\n| C47 | `load_png_mem` | no `IEND`; `IEND` before the IDATs; trailing garbage after `IEND` | [x] |\n| C48 | `load_png_mem` | `png_length` longer than the real file (extra bytes readable) and exactly the file length | [x] |\n| C4